# gui-toolbox domain structure

Organize feature code by domain under `src/domains/`.

## Layout

```
src/
  app/                  # app shell wiring only
  domains/
    scripts/
    translator/
    keybinds/
    settings/
  shared/
    ui/                 # shadcn components
    components/         # reusable app UI (shell, page frame, etc.)
    hooks/              # reusable hooks
    lib/                # pure utilities (e.g. cn)
    model.ts            # shared types / constants
```

## Domain folder conventions

Each feature domain (`scripts`, `translator`, `keybinds`, `settings`) should contain:

- `views/` — page-level UI only (compose components + hooks)
- `components/` — domain UI pieces (display / interaction only)
- `hooks/` — business / state / side-effect logic
- `model.ts` — types and pure domain helpers when needed
- `index.ts` — public exports for the domain

## Rules

1. Views and components must not own persistence, IPC, or catalog orchestration — put that in hooks (or plain modules called by hooks).
2. Put reusable cross-domain UI/logic in `shared/`, not inside a feature domain.
3. Put shadcn primitives in `shared/ui`; prefer adding via `bunx --bun shadcn@latest add`.
4. Prefer importing from a domain’s `index.ts` when crossing domain boundaries.
